Review the uncommitted changes in src/metal/metal_server.cpp (git diff; the q27_kernels.metal/metal_backend.mm/README changes are separate reviewed rounds — ignore them). This is a FIX-VERIFICATION round: a previous review of this same diff (the /v1/responses full port of src/server.cu:1441-1882 onto Runtime::run + Runtime::EngineError split) found no P1 and three findings, all addressed in the current working tree:

1. (P2) Text→think interleavings corrupted output_index: BOTH the streaming route and the non-stream route now flush pending text BEFORE accumulating think on a THINK transition (same rule as the TOOL branch). Verify the transition matrix is now complete (text→think, think→text, text→tool, tool→text, think→tool, tool→think) for out_index/msg_index integrity in the stream path and item ordering in the non-stream path.

2. (P2) Non-stream bare-call recovery returned both the raw JSON text and the recovered call: recovery now runs BEFORE flush_text, scans the UNCOMMITTED `text` buffer instead of text_accum, applies the tx=pre convention, and flushes the pre-call prose message before pushing the calls. Verify: no double-emission, no lost prose, item ordering matches model output order, and the recorded coarseness (a bare call split across a think/tool transition stays surfaced as committed text) is actually bounded to that case.

3. (P3) Streaming engine-failure path left an unterminated lifecycle: item state + flush machinery hoisted above the try; the catch(std::exception) now closes any open item via the normal flushers, emits the api_error event, then a response.failed terminator carrying last_error + partial output. Verify: no use-before-declaration, no event that can throw through the catch, no double done-triplet, flushers are no-ops when nothing is open, and response.failed is spec-shaped (status failed + last_error{code,message} + output).

Also re-check the round's original concerns still hold after the edits: EngineError cannot leak uncaught through the streaming provider; the 400 class is not widened; bare-call recovery still runs with empty tools. P1/P2/P3 verdicts with file:line.

