./docs/METAL_PROGRESS.md:315:**Parity audit adopted x2 + a probe-found server gap fixed; B1 quality battery FULL PASS through our stack; E6 measured: FUND ONE ROUND (2026-07-16/17 night, quiet 24 GB M4 + yukon).** External CUDA/Metal parity audit: both LOW findings source-verified REAL and fixed same night (triage: `docs/plans/2026-07-17-parity-audit-triage.md`) — (A) every CUDA argmax-family reduction tie-broke to the HIGHEST index vs Metal/CPU's lowest; `am_pack` now packs `~idx` so one rule holds everywhere, tie assertions added to the CUDA battery, ALL PASS on yukon (oracle swapped and restored exactly, 23,224 MiB); (B) top-p dropped exact boundary ties that CUDA keeps — both CPU paths now extend through value ties, three-way-tie test fails pre-fix. Probing found a third, unlisted gap: **the Metal server never rendered `tools` into the prompt** (constrainer triggers only) — `tools_preamble` extracted to shared `tool_preamble.h`, Metal merges it like `chatml_prompt`, CUDA rebuild verified. **B1 Phase 0A-q27 (pre-registered bands, then run): quality reproduced through OUR engine** — 8K wikitext NLL B1/T2 = 1.055 (band [1.05,1.30]), B1/official = 2.28x (≤3.5x); recorded-prompt probes 4/4 machine-checked (toolcall passing AFTER the server fix — the probe earned its keep); decode 17.3/17.1 tok/s artifact = CONDITIONAL band (≥18 strong), resident ceiling 19.16 tok/s @ 69 GB/s (T2 same-bench: 11.54 @ 78.5) → **one B1 kernel look funded, ship ≥18 artifact**. `metal_decode_bench --dtype b1` added. **E6 run: R = 0.716 → FUND ONE ROUND** (52.44/73.24 GB/s; attn q 0.517 and ssm/attn out 0.572 worst, ffn pair 0.731 at 43.9% of bytes; parity prize ~1.4x serial decode). Two funded kernel rounds now queued behind explicit go: B1 select round 2, Q4 official rewrite (ship R ≥ 0.90).
./docs/METAL_PROGRESS.md:323:**Metal server agentic parity SHIPPED: tool loops work end-to-end — pi read-tool smoke PASS, all 8 pre-registered gates green (2026-07-17, 24 GB M4; Daniel's go: "Go for the parity pass").** An external review named seven agentic blockers in the Metal API; all seven source-verified REAL, plus an eighth found in verification that mattered most for this box: the OpenAI chat endpoint (pi's API) also emitted no structured tool_calls — the model's <tool_call> XML arrived as plain content text, so pi's tool loop was structurally broken (yesterday's B1 "toolcall probe PASS" validated model emission, not API delivery). The fix was a wiring port, not a design round (`docs/plans/2026-07-17-metal-agentic-parity.md`): metal_server.cpp now consumes `api_common.h` wholesale (stream_format.h's verbatim Utf8Gate copy deduped away) — **/v1/messages** gets full server.cu parity (anthropic_msgs/anthropic_tools_json mapping with incoming tool_use/tool_result/thinking reconstruction and billing-header normalization, StreamSplitter routing into thinking/text/tool_use blocks with input_json_delta streaming + bare-call recovery, stop_reason tool_use, Anthropic error envelope, and the pre-slot "prompt is too long" 400 that Claude Code keys compaction off), **/v1/messages/count_tokens** lands (CPU-only, counts exactly what /v1/messages prefills), and **/v1/chat/completions goes beyond CUDA** (whose chat endpoint is text-only by design): incoming assistant.tool_calls/role:"tool" mapped to the model's markers, outgoing message.tool_calls + full-wire-shape streaming delta.tool_calls with finish_reason tool_calls, <think> to reasoning_content — closing the registered think-leak residue on both endpoints (responses still flattens; residue). Context preflight on all four endpoints in each API's native shape. Renderer switch to shared `chatml_prompt` verified byte-safe first (strip_chatml ≡ strip_ctrl; added-token encode) and brings the CUDA default-system over-refusal fix along. Evidence (`logs/agentic-parity-20260717/`): count_tokens == usage.input_tokens exact; tool_use + input_json_delta both modes; tool_result round-trip consumed; billing pair full prefix hit 539/539; oversized prompt answers "prompt is too long: 140020 tokens > 131039 maximum"; **pi 0.80.10 executed a real read-tool loop against the server** — the retry that was impossible the night before. Codex: no P1; all four findings adopted (Anthropic error envelope via anthropic_guarded, per-endpoint max_tokens defaults 1024/256/4096 matching CUDA, gate wire-shape tightening). Gate-authoring lesson: curl -d without a Content-Type is form-urlencoded and httplib caps THAT at 8 KB → 413; real JSON clients are uncapped. Registered residue: /v1/responses structured function_call items; error-class split (engine failures on /v1/messages should be api_error 500); CUDA chat could adopt openai_msgs at the next merge.
