P2: [src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1860](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1860) / [src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1888](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1888)  
Non-stream bare-call recovery is not bounded only to calls split across a think/tool transition. The route now flushes any pending text before `THINK` and `TOOL`, but recovery only scans the final uncommitted `text` buffer at the end. A complete bare call emitted as text and then followed by `<think>` or `<tool_call>` is committed as a raw message before recovery runs, so it will not become a `function_call`. Example shape: `{"name":"Bash","arguments":{...}}<think>...` yields raw JSON text plus reasoning, no recovered call, even though the call was not split. To make the coarseness match the comment, recovery needs to run inside the text flush path before committing each text segment.

P3: none found.

Other verification notes: the streaming transition matrix now preserves `out_index/msg_index` for text->think, think->text, text->tool, tool->text, think->tool, and tool->think. The streaming failure path has the lifecycle state in scope, closes open think/text items before `response.failed`, and `ev()` itself records write failure rather than throwing on normal sink failure. `EngineError` is caught by the streaming provider through `std::exception`, non-stream `engine_guard` only wraps `run()`, so validation/overflow still stay 400-class, and bare-call recovery still runs with empty `tools` via the `nullptr` parser path.
